In this question you will be assessed on using good English, organising information clearly and using specialist terms where appropriate.
A dairy farmer washes out his cow shed each day.
The waste water contains urine and faeces.
The waste water overflows into a stream by mistake.
The waste water will have an effect on the plants and invertebrates living in the stream.
Part (a): Explain why.','Urine and faeces add mineral ions and organic matter to the stream.
Algae and aquatic plants grow rapidly.
Dense growth blocks light, so submerged plants cannot photosynthesise and die.
Decomposers feed on the dead material and respire.
Dissolved oxygen falls.
Invertebrates and other aquatic organisms may die from oxygen shortage.
This process is eutrophication.','["Urine and faeces add mineral ions and organic matter to the stream.","Algae and aquatic plants grow rapidly.","Dense growth blocks light, so submerged plants cannot photosynthesise and die.","Decomposers feed on the dead material and respire.","Dissolved oxygen falls.","Invertebrates and other aquatic organisms may die from oxygen shortage.","This process is eutrophication."]'::jsonb,6,'AO2','Explain','Both / not separated','Grades 7–9','4.7.3',3,true) on conflict (id) do update set question=excluded.question, model_answer=excluded.model_answer, marking_points=excluded.marking_points, active=true;
